  "graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "m29_intro",
        "type": "flograph.util.note",
        "pos": [
          0,
          -460
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "# Model canvases\n\nA big flow doesn't have to live on one surface. This one uses both kinds\nof canvas tab.\n\n- **Clean the orders** is a frame turned into a *model canvas*: the small\n  box stands for the steps inside it. **Double-click the box** to open\n  them. Its edges are declared ports, `orders` in and `paid orders` out \u2014\n  right-click it \u25b8 **Inputs and Outputs\u2026** to choose and name them.\n- **Summaries** is still a frame, with a tab of its own on the page bar:\n  the same nodes, fenced off, so a click or a drag-select only lands on\n  what is in it.\n\nRight-click the box \u25b8 **Turn back into a Frame** to bring the steps back\nout; one **Ctrl+Z** undoes either conversion.",
          "width": 560,
          "height": 280
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null,
        "description": "",
        "active": true,
        "locked": false,
        "frozen": false,
        "manual": false,
        "frozen_fingerprint": null,
        "exclusive": null,
        "preview": true,
        "port_labels": null,
